  "implementation": [
    "While every stored row has series[index].series_id==index, charge one checked unit and use id<len as a hit, otherwise absence.",
    "Initialize/reset proof on new/successful begin; update after successful label copy and row append; a nonpositional append permanently selects the unchanged generic scan until the next begin.",
    "Invalidate before fallible Matrix sort, including interruption after swaps. Preserve first labels, point arrival order, equal-label distinct IDs, copy ownership, abort/take/rebegin and independent result release.",
    "No output renumbering, metadata owner, value array or additional raw buffering. Rust collect and C convenience collection use this owner; Netdata HTTP streaming has its own indexed lookup."
  ],
